Commit:     Fabricio Breve <fbreve@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Thu Oct 22 20:17:38 2026 -0300

    Preserve CPU restart context across savestates
    
    Preserve the prefix and EI restart context required for exact CPU execution after savestate restore.
    
    Extend the tagged savestate format to version 13 and restore the instruction context needed by the canonical T80 restart sequence.
    
    Prevent prefixed instructions and EI interrupt-delay state from being lost across LOAD, including block instructions such as LDIR.
    
    Add accepted-boundary, prefix, block-instruction, EI, HALT, repeated-load, and CPU restart regression coverage.

